{
  "concepts": [
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "F16, Engagement baseline, is an operational profile whose entry choice is direct engagement or coordination. It imports F1 frames/context, F2 transitions/steps/configuration, F3 results/combination, F4 work state/resumption/reuse, F5 proportionality/cost, F6 claims/evidence/assessment/acceptance, F15 Product lineage and F13 work carriers. Imported consequences retain their owners.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 219,
          "quote": "rules that state them keep their owners, and the choice column names them\nas imported, never as this profile's choices.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F3.%20Engagement%20applicability%2FFoundation%20to%20law",
          "start_line": 218
        }
      ],
      "key": "engagement_baseline",
      "label": "Engagement baseline"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "A trace of profile rules to commitments, imported consequences, instance premises and separately owned policy choices, with consumer loci. The source describes P0 as recovered; P1, P2, P3, P4a and P6 as independent; P4b as derived from P0 and P2 under non-reacquirable step facts; and P5 as derived from P0 and P6 under an open-world premise. The trace is new in this corpus, has no rc.2 row, adds no rule and binds no axiomatic-calculus rule.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 223,
          "quote": "P2, P3, P4a and P6 independent; P4b derived from P0 and P2, with P0's\npremise that step-produced facts are not re-acquirable; P5 derived from P0\nand P6, with P0's open-world premise.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F3.%20Engagement%20applicability%2FFoundation%20to%20law",
          "start_line": 221
        },
        {
          "end_line": 291,
          "quote": "No row\nnames pillar 10, axiomatic calculus: this profile states no rule of the\na_c calculus and binds none.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F3.%20Engagement%20applicability%2FFoundation%20to%20law",
          "start_line": 289
        }
      ],
      "key": "foundation_trace",
      "label": "Foundation-to-law trace"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "A frame whose evaluation family concerns selecting, constructing, assessing or disposing governed work. Executive, Worker and Reviewer are this profile's engagement frames.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 341,
          "quote": "An engagement frame is a frame (REFERENCE_FRAME §1) whose evaluation family\nconcerns selecting, constructing, assessing or disposing governed work.\nExecutive, Worker and Reviewer are this profile's engagement frames",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FEngagement%20frame",
          "start_line": 339
        }
      ],
      "key": "engagement_frame",
      "label": "Engagement frame"
    },
    {
      "conditions": ["Needed by one engagement evaluation and activated."],
      "definition": "A Product, requirement, design, identity, release, domain, implementation, test, operational, historical or capability frame.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 348,
          "quote": "A specialist frame is an activated Product, requirement, design, identity,\nrelease, domain, implementation, test, operational, historical or\ncapability frame that one engagement evaluation needs.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FSpecialist%20frame",
          "start_line": 346
        }
      ],
      "key": "specialist_frame",
      "label": "Specialist frame"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "A reusable evaluation-family archetype naming a recurring distinction. It selects no concrete carrier, component, actor, architecture, owner or implementation.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 360,
          "quote": "A generic specialist-frame family is a reusable evaluation-family archetype\nof this profile (§11). It names a recurring distinction that a project\neither instantiates where material, has capable authority establish as\nnon-material for the governed outcome, or keeps as an explicit coverage\nresidual",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FGeneric%20specialist-frame%20family",
          "start_line": 356
        }
      ],
      "key": "generic_specialist_family",
      "label": "Generic specialist-frame family"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Testing frame, authoritative Product path and material combinatorial complexity are tier-2 terms owned by ASSURANCE §7; this profile imports their definitions without additions.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 372,
          "quote": "Testing frame, authoritative Product path and material combinatorial\ncomplexity are tier-2 terms defined in ASSURANCE §7. This profile uses them\nas defined there and adds nothing to them",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FTerms%20owned%20by%20ASSURANCE",
          "start_line": 370
        }
      ],
      "key": "assurance_owned_terms",
      "label": "ASSURANCE-owned terms"
    },
    {
      "conditions": ["Acts under existing project decision authority."],
      "definition": "The engagement frame selecting or confirming bounded activation configurations and consuming closed Worker and Reviewer results. Its complete Product view and current MVP or release mandate support priority, disposition and next authorised action. This view is not the complete workspace or every evaluator's context.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 382,
          "quote": "Executive is this profile's label for the frame that selects or confirms\nthe bounded activation configuration and consumes closed Worker and\nReviewer results under existing project decision authority. It holds the\ncomplete Product view and the current MVP or release mandate needed to\nassign priority, apply disposition and select the next authorised action",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FExecutive",
          "start_line": 377
        }
      ],
      "key": "executive",
      "label": "Executive"
    },
    {
      "conditions": ["Activated as a frame within exact intake and inherited operation authority."],
      "definition": "The constructor role owning bounded construction and self-review. Writer is its specialisation for documents and records.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 395,
          "quote": "Worker is this profile's label for the constructor role of ACTIVATION §1\nactivated as a frame. It owns construction and self-review inside its exact\nintake, through the operation authority inherited from the governing work\nrelation.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FWorker",
          "start_line": 392
        },
        {
          "end_line": 768,
          "quote": "It allocates construction to the Worker frame, specialised as Writer for\ndocuments and records;",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F7.%20Non-hierarchical%20frame%20configuration%2FThe%20executive%20configuration",
          "start_line": 767
        }
      ],
      "key": "worker",
      "label": "Worker / Writer"
    },
    {
      "conditions": ["Separately activated where independent assessment is required."],
      "definition": "An independent live-surface evaluation frame consumed by the assessment relation. It evaluates one exact subject and returns a closed result with evidence-bound technical triage when a finding exists, under imported independence, traceability, assurance-boundary and qualification-freeze rules.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 405,
          "quote": "Reviewer is this profile's label for the independent live-surface\nevaluation that the assessment relation of ACTIVATION §1 consumes, governed\nby EVALUATION §3 (independence and traceability) and EVALUATION §1 and §7\n(assurance boundary and qualification freeze), activated as a frame. It\nevaluates one exact subject and returns a closed result, with evidence-bound\ntechnical triage when a finding exists.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FReviewer",
          "start_line": 400
        }
      ],
      "key": "reviewer",
      "label": "Reviewer"
    },
    {
      "conditions": ["Against one exact evaluated claim and basis."],
      "definition": "The Reviewer's assessment of a finding: affected claim and observed failure; Product-scale severity; causal assessment and quantified-assurance confidence; blast radius and affected users, paths or relations; available workaround or containment; repair complexity, regression risk and material dependencies; residual uncertainty and evidence that would reduce it. Fields are supported only within admissible evidence and actor capability.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 414,
          "quote": "Technical triage is the Reviewer's assessment of one finding against the\nexact evaluated claim and basis. Where admissible evidence and the actor's\ncapability envelope support it, the triage records",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FTechnical%20triage%2C%20severity%2C%20priority%20and%20boundary%20effect",
          "start_line": 411
        }
      ],
      "key": "technical_triage",
      "label": "Technical triage"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Severity grades a finding's consequence if manifested and is Reviewer evaluation evidence. Priority orders response by complete Product outcome, likelihood, exposure, current MVP or release mandate, reversibility, dependencies, cost of delay and capacity; it is assigned by the Executive. These remain distinct from the frame result and boundary effect even where policy maps between them.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 434,
          "quote": "Severity grades the consequence if the finding manifests. Priority orders\nthe response relative to the complete Product outcome, likelihood and\nexposure, the current MVP or release mandate, reversibility, dependencies,\ncost of delay and available capacity. The Reviewer grades severity; the\nExecutive assigns priority",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FTechnical%20triage%2C%20severity%2C%20priority%20and%20boundary%20effect",
          "start_line": 430
        }
      ],
      "key": "severity_and_priority",
      "label": "Severity and priority"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The Executive's recorded decision projection for one finding at the current promotion boundary: blocks, requires narrowing, or may remain an explicit residual. It is neither a result nor a disposition, maps to no core value itself and decides nothing by itself.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 456,
          "quote": "Current-boundary effect is the Executive's recorded determination of what\none finding does to the current promotion boundary: it blocks it, requires\nnarrowing it, or may remain an explicit residual. It is a decision\nprojection, a state this profile declares, not a result and not a\ndisposition (§8): it maps to no core value of its own and decides nothing\nby itself.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FTechnical%20triage%2C%20severity%2C%20priority%20and%20boundary%20effect",
          "start_line": 451
        }
      ],
      "key": "current_boundary_effect",
      "label": "Current-boundary effect"
    },
    {
      "conditions": ["Exists only after successful Worker activation."],
      "definition": "The Worker's closed output to its declared consumer, the Executive in the coordinated branch. Its construction-availability refinement has five values: candidate_ready→satisfied; refused→falsified; incomplete→falsified; re_entry_requested(authority)→out_of_frame; re_entry_requested(basis)→invalid_basis. After lawful activation the imported mapping is total and exclusive for 'a candidate is available'. These carriers are neither assessment, acceptance nor new dispositions.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 474,
          "quote": "A work result is the Worker's closed output to its declared consumer; in\nthe coordinated branch that consumer is the Executive. It exists only after\na successful Worker activation.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FWork%20result",
          "start_line": 472
        },
        {
          "end_line": 490,
          "quote": "maps each to exactly one core value, and states that the mapping is total\nand exclusive after lawful activation. In this profile they are carriers,\nnot new semantic dispositions, and none of them is an assessment or an\nacceptance of the candidate",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FWork%20result",
          "start_line": 487
        }
      ],
      "key": "work_result",
      "label": "Work result"
    },
    {
      "conditions": ["A mismatch is known during activation."],
      "definition": "A refusal of activation carrying the cause and owner-defined core value to the assigning authority or declared carrier. It creates no active Worker frame, Worker evaluation or Worker result; capability, authority, subject, stale or ambiguous basis and topology mismatches belong here when detected at activation.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 478,
          "quote": "returns to the assigning authority or declared result carrier and creates\nneither a Worker activation nor a Worker result.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FWork%20result",
          "start_line": 477
        }
      ],
      "key": "activation_refusal",
      "label": "Activation refusal"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The exact subject identity required by transition evidence and traceability, stabilised sufficiently for the claimed assessment. Generic method qualification requires freezing its construction result before material reference exposure; elsewhere immutable identity or an equivalent exact-subject relation suffices. No lifecycle state named frozen is created.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 536,
          "quote": "An exact candidate is the subject identity that the transition evidence of\nACTIVATION §7 and the traceability of EVALUATION §3 require. Where generic\nmethod qualification applies (EVALUATION §7), its construction result is\nfrozen before material reference exposure as that clause requires.\nElsewhere this profile stabilises the review subject through an immutable\nidentity or an equivalent exact-subject relation sufficient for the claimed\nassessment. The profile creates no new lifecycle state named `frozen`",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FExact%20candidate",
          "start_line": 529
        }
      ],
      "key": "exact_candidate",
      "label": "Exact candidate"
    },
    {
      "conditions": ["The Product-owned basis adopts this profile."],
      "definition": "A projection inside the Product-owned Project Reference-Frame Basis recording selected profile mapping, exact outcome, actor envelopes, evidence coordinates and revision conditions additional to the Product binding. It is not a second basis and creates no authority.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 545,
          "quote": "A baseline-adoption projection consumes the Product-owned Project\nReference-Frame Basis of PRODUCT_DEFINITION §7. Where that basis adopts\nthis profile, the projection records the selected profile mapping, exact\noutcome, actor envelopes, evidence coordinates and revision conditions\nneeded in addition to the Product binding (§16). It is not a second\nframe-basis definition and mints none of the authority it projects",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FBaseline-adoption%20projection",
          "start_line": 540
        }
      ],
      "key": "baseline_adoption_projection",
      "label": "Baseline-adoption projection"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The Product-owned record projecting existing outcome/work-authority decisions and profile adoption, citing every material authority source without merging those sources into local-axiom authority.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 1129,
          "quote": "The Product-owned Project Reference-Frame Basis\n(PRODUCT_DEFINITION §7) projects that decision",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F12.%20Complete%20engagement%20transition%2F1.%20Existing%20authority%20selects%20the%20basis",
          "start_line": 1128
        }
      ],
      "key": "project_reference_frame_basis",
      "label": "Project Reference-Frame Basis"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "An Executive attention procedure over U, initially every known material evaluation not closed on the current basis. It selects finite dependency-ready activations M fitting assigned actors and tracks the frontier and closed-result ledger rather than evaluators' undocumented context.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 599,
          "quote": "U0 = every known material evaluation not closed on the current basis\n\nwhile U is non-empty:\n  select a finite dependency-ready subset M that fits the assigned actors\n  activate each member of M against the exact outcome and basis\n  keep assurance-independent evaluations free of unclosed peer results",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F6.%20Executive%20attention%2C%20evaluation%20and%20action%2FAttention%20cycle",
          "start_line": 594
        }
      ],
      "key": "attention_cycle",
      "label": "Attention cycle"
    },
    {
      "conditions": ["Revalidated before activation and before disposition."],
      "definition": "Five locks: outcome—unchanged selected Goal, outcome, boundary, lawful re-entry class, MVP/release mandate and triage policy; basis—exact/current subject, authority, dependency, configuration, topology, evidence, time and candidate coordinates; Product-role—distinct mutable Source Project, Product Definition, Release Cut, Product, Install, Artifact and dependent Product with each Development Product bound to its exact Install; authority—unchanged semantic, evaluation, operation, decision, acceptance and publication owners/grants; coverage-and-return—each material evaluation/interaction closed or explicit residual and each consumed result following its declared return.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 667,
          "quote": "Before activation and before disposition, the Executive revalidates five\nlocks",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F6.%20Executive%20attention%2C%20evaluation%20and%20action%2FDrift%20locks",
          "start_line": 666
        }
      ],
      "key": "drift_locks",
      "label": "Drift locks"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "A governed outcome concerns one Product or an explicitly directed Product chain. Its basis distinguishes every mutable Source Project, current Product Definition, exact candidate checkpoint, Release Cut, Product, Install, Artifact, Development Product, dependent Product and composition edge. Each Development Product role binds exactly one underlying Install.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 700,
          "quote": "A governed outcome may concern one Product or an explicit directed chain of\nProducts. Its basis records the distinct role of every mutable Source\nProject, current Product Definition, exact candidate checkpoint, Release\nCut, Product, Install, Artifact, Development Product, dependent Product and\ncomposition edge. Each Development Product role binds one exact underlying\nInstall identity.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F6.%20Executive%20attention%2C%20evaluation%20and%20action%2FProduct-chain%20basis",
          "start_line": 695
        }
      ],
      "key": "product_chain_basis",
      "label": "Product-chain basis"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Distinct structures used by the configuration: authority precedence selects lawful decision surfaces; temporal/evidence flow carries activation packets and closed results; frame topology records disjointness, overlap, conjunction, translation and composition. Evaluation independence and Reviewer assurance independence remain separate activation relations.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 737,
          "quote": "3. frame topology records disjointness, overlap, conjunction, translation\n   or composition among the evaluations actually used (REFERENCE_FRAME §7),\n   while evaluation independence and Reviewer assurance independence stay\n   separate activation relations.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F7.%20Non-hierarchical%20frame%20configuration",
          "start_line": 734
        }
      ],
      "key": "frame_relation_structures",
      "label": "Non-hierarchical relation structures"
    },
    {
      "conditions": ["Selected where bounded change and delivery across successive tasks need separate attention."],
      "definition": "One lawful configuration allocating construction to Worker/Writer, required assessment to Reviewer and coordination/disposition within an admitted existing decision grant to Executive. It is neither the method default nor a role inventory required for every task.",
      "exceptions": ["Where one sufficient frame covers the task, direct entry applies."],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 775,
          "quote": "It is\none configuration, selected where it fits the task, not an inventory of\nroles that all work needs. Existing authority selects it or another\nconfiguration under §16, and a configuration with other frames, names or\ntopology is evaluated against its own task as ACTIVATION §1 Configuration\nstates, not by its distance from this one",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F7.%20Non-hierarchical%20frame%20configuration%2FThe%20executive%20configuration",
          "start_line": 770
        }
      ],
      "key": "executive_configuration",
      "label": "Executive configuration"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The smallest real runnable path from a supported Product entry to a material outcome through the selected composition. This profile's delivery strategy establishes it early and widens it through bounded increments selected by consequential uncertainty, dependency/interface reach and failure impact. Its rationale is early end-to-end feedback at the cost of later widening.",
      "exceptions": ["If a thread already exists, extend or revalidate the affected thread."],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 879,
          "quote": "The Executive sequences delivery around a steel thread: the smallest real,\nrunnable path from a supported Product entry to a material outcome through\nthe selected composition. The path is established early and widened in\nbounded increments; where it already exists, the affected thread is extended\nor revalidated. Increments are chosen for consequential uncertainty,\ndependency and interface reach, and failure impact",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F8.%20Derived%20Executive%20frame%2FSteel-thread%20delivery",
          "start_line": 873
        }
      ],
      "key": "steel_thread",
      "label": "Steel-thread delivery"
    },
    {
      "conditions": ["Interpreted in urn:stdo:bounded-context:reference-frame-evaluation under the selected basis."],
      "definition": "Product archetype: evaluate one exact current Product claim, outcome, boundary and lifecycle against current Intent, Product, requirements, acceptance meaning and coordinates. Product/requirement authority retain meaning and acceptance; output is bounded evaluation and evidence. Immediate falsifier: design, code, tests, predecessor behaviour or local convention changes Product meaning or substitutes the subject.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 1019,
          "quote": "Product and requirement authority keep meaning and acceptance. The frame returns only a bounded evaluation result and evidence.",
