      ],
      "key": "profile_premises_and_ownership",
      "statement": "I1 assumes bounded tasks under one outcome with construction and cross-task delivery needing separate attention; I2 locates every decision grant in existing project authority; I3 assumes fallible finite-context actors, possibly probabilistic constructors. These are adopted instance premises, not foundational consequences. The profile owns only added terms/choices; conflicting owning clauses control. Inclusion makes it available, not adopted. Names convey only allocated responsibilities. Consumers decide nothing beyond owning rules. The table traces the lead and §§1–22; ASSURANCE-owned terms, the trace itself and §23 dispositions add no rules. The source's pillars 1–9 do not confer calculus authority.",
